nters with my  colleague on the breakfast wrote us  uh or previously my colleague on the  breakfast wrote is piers morgan you'll  have  noted you know he has this morning you  know  not apologized for what he said and  indeed has has stuck to his guns he has  i tweeted this morning i'm reliably  informed you know i continue to believe  that which i said which was of course  that he didn't believe meghan markle  when she spoke about her suicidal  thoughts i just wondered  what you made of that well uh putting  the issue  aside and of um what he was actually  talking about i'll miss the interviews  with with him i would have been doing  one in  and half an hour or whatever time i'm on  good morning britain this morning and  uh personally i always thought he he  gave a very tough but usually quite fair  interview and as with all interviewee  interviewers i was fine if you actually  answered the question  he tended to have an okay ride with it  which  which  was always uh you know i was trying to  go on and just if you didn't know the  answer just say  look i don't know or if you do know or  you know um  you you you give the facts um so uh  personally i'll miss him  uh on there uh i wasn't gonna get into  the details of the argument one way or  the other with regard to  uh uh megan though and that that's right  the different matter  uh why not i mean i'm sorry i mean you  know it's a yeah  a prominent broadcaster essentially said  on television that he did not believe  at someone when they spoke about their  mental health  now at a time of course when we're all  very preoccupied  with our own mental health be you a  royal or a commoner like myself  i i just wonder why you wouldn't speak  specifically to that  yeah first of all mental health is  incredibly  important and particularly during this  pandemic even more so  and there are two things here really  first of all there's a long-standing i  think very good convention that cabinet  ministers don't um sort of comment 